cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VoxRigor in research, please cite this software and the specific version or commit you used."
title: "VoxRigor: Open-Source Voice Authentication Security Testing and Evaluation Framework"
authors:
  - name: "AB772K"
version: "0.1.0.dev0"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AB772K/VoxRigor"
abstract: >-
  VoxRigor is an early-stage, local-first framework for reproducible research
  and authorized security evaluation of voice-authentication systems. The
  current Phase 1 prototype provides project manifests, a diagnostic test
  runner, provenance metadata, and JSON/HTML reporting. Biometric evaluation,
  audio testing, model adapters, and target-application testing are planned
  roadmap capabilities and are not yet implemented.
keywords:
  - voice biometrics
  - speaker verification
  - presentation attack detection
  - security research
  - authentication security
